acceptance_criteria: "Exercise real nested extension help and command execution; Render every supported flag once with one coherent value placeholder; Preserve published legacy spelling support and modern value_name descriptors; Keep shared validation, parsing, structured help and author guidance coherent"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Shared SDK long-name and scalar-kind resolution now keeps help, dispatch and runtime contracts coherent. Boolean inline labels are suppressed, explicit value_name compatibility is retained, and unknown inherited kind names reject."
expected_result: "Canonical flag identity uses one SDK rule; valid boolean declarations stay value-free and machine-readable, explicit metadata and kind precedence remain compatible, and unknown kinds return null."
actual_result: "Both CodeRabbit findings are corrected through shared SDK primitives: one long-name resolver owns supported canonical identity and trimmed legacy fallback across all help, dispatch and contract sites; boolean inline labels are omitted from contracts while explicit value_name compatibility and declared-kind precedence remain. The existing scalar-kind resolver canonicalizes supported dynamic aliases and now rejects inherited constructor/__proto__ entries through an own-key lookup. Real public contract and inherited-kind controls fail before correction and pass afterward. All149 focused cases pass, including real CLI bool-alias presence and typed/native/legacy/untyped projections. All4 linked commands pass. Complete static validation passes, and the full suite passes10,409 tests with3 explicit skips at exact100% lines65067/65067, statements68493/68493, functions14116/14116 and branches52545/52545. Coverage scope,100% thresholds and workflows remain unchanged; branch counts reflect the actual shared-kind refactor, not exclusions. The surface adds one classified name resolver to the earlier12 additive exports. Renewed hosted checks and full bot review are required before merge."
